[agent] I found a clear bug in the CLI: at `fg.py:1094` it calls `index.add_embedding(EmbeddingFeature(...))`, but the SDK signature is `add_embedding(name, dimension, similarity_function_type, ...)`. It passes an `EmbeddingFeature` object as the `name` arg, leaving `dimension` unfilled → crash. This is a trivial argument-marshalling bug in the CLI wrapper (the underlying SDK/platform fully supports L2 vector search). I'll fix this one-line marshalling error so the interface can do its job, and document it.
