[agent] The ordering is correct (OpenSearch returns highest `_score` first; the transform `1/_score - 1` is monotonically decreasing, so the list is nearest-first). But the negative score values are suspicious — for a true L2 space, `1/_score - 1` would be a non-negative distance. Negative values imply `_score > 1`, which L2 space never produces. I need to confirm the index actually uses L2 and not cosine. Let me check how `l2_norm` maps to the OpenSearch space type.
